OSF DCE Features & Functionality

Length   1 day  Revision 1.1

Who should attend
Technical professionals who require a high level of understanding of
the
latest release of OSF's DCE.  This class is for application developers,
system engineers, network administrators, strategic planners, technical
managers, support engineers, and technical marketers.  This seminar is
a
prerequisite for all other DCE seminars and courses from OSF.

Course Summary
The new OSF DCE Features and Functionality technical seminar has been
updated to meet the challenging needs of the DCE audience.  In addition
to
architectural overview information on DCE, this seminar focuses on
explaining the issues in the computer industry that drove the need for
DCE
and how DCE provides an effective solution for these problems.  This
seminar provides an example of how DCE can be implemented in a typical
corporate environment which includes legacy systems as well as new DCE
platforms.  The seminar, which introduces the component services of OSF
DCE
version 1.1, also will  illustrate a DCE cell configuration and provide
an
overview of how a typical distributed application works within the
cell.
At the completion of this course the student will be able to define
modern
distributed computing challenges, give a high level description of the
OSF
DCE architecture, name and describe the component services of DCE and
describe how DCE services work together to provide DCE functionality.

