Or possibly the shar file has a preamble, which "unshar"
would skip, but which "sh" is objecting to.

Look in the shar file and see if there are any lines at the
start of the file which DON'T begin with `#'.

If so, strip them out until the first line beginning with `#'
and try again.  Or use/get "unshar".

