organization: Amherst College, Amherst MA, USA
newsgroups: comp.unix.osf.misc

If you're using both NIS and enhanced security, the protect password
info for NIS users is not in /tcb/files/auth anymore, but combined
into one file, /var/yp/src/prpasswd, from which, if you do "make
prpasswd" in the /var/yp directory, the relevent database files are
created in /var/yp/NIS-DOMAIN-NAME.  It's important that you remove
all the files in /tcb/files/auth for everybody covered by NIS.  You
have problems if somebody is in both prpasswd and the /tcb/files/auth
files.  To remove redundant local files, DEC suggested the following
script.

#!/usr/bin/ksh -ph
ypcat -k prpasswd | cut -d' ' -f1 | while read user ; do
    let="${user%${user#?}}"
    file="/tcb/files/auth/$let/$user"
    [ -f "$file" ] && rm -f "$file"
done

Assuming that I didn't make a typing error, this script goes through
the prpasswd file, checks to see if there is a file in /tcb/files/auth
for the same user, and removes it if there is.

